Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 20:36:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] docs(mcp): correct catalog and plugin MCP install docs

Four MCP install/connect descriptions no longer match the code on main:

- tool-search.md said manage_connections is present whether or not you
  are signed in because it also installs catalog MCP servers. The tool is
  registered with check_fn=connectors_available (tools/connectors/tool.py),
  which needs tools.connectors.enabled plus a free-tier identity or a
  Portal token carrying the managed_tools claim; everyone else never sees
  it.
- mcp.md said non-secret catalog values go to ~/.hermes/.env, and the
  Asana example showed both OAuth credentials as ${VAR} refs. install_entry
  (hermes_cli/mcp_catalog.py) saves only secrets to .env and inlines every
  secret: false value into the mcp_servers block (_inline_non_secret_value);
  the Asana manifest declares ASANA_CLIENT_ID secret: false.
- plugins_activation/plugins_loader docstrings, plugins/AGENTS.md and the
  plugin developer guide said a mid-run plugin's MCP servers wait for
  "mcp.reload" (no such RPC; the RPC is reload.mcp, the command
  /reload-mcp). Install surfaces run load_and_go_live, which connects them
  in place and reports them as live_now.mcp_servers; only a process that
  did not run it (the messaging gateway) still waits for /reload-mcp.
  gateway-internals.md carried the same stale name.

Docs and docstrings only; no behaviour change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
